## Why This Is Asked

Examines practical handling of delayed supervision, distribution drift, and safe deployment in production ML systems.

## Key Concepts

- Delayed feedback and label latency
- Concept drift and drift detectors (ADWIN-like)
- Online vs offline retraining
- Calibration and evaluation (AUROC, PR-AUC, FPR)
- Data/versioning and deployment safety

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation sketch
let model = initModel();
let buffer = [];
stream.on('event', async (e) => {
  const x = featuresFromEvent(e);
  const yHat = model.predict(x);
  storePrediction(e.id, yHat);
  buffer.push({id: e.id, x, timestamp: Date.now()});
});

// Drift detection
setInterval(() => {
  const recent = getRecentPredictions(window);
  const metrics = evaluateMetrics(recent);
  if (driftDetector.detect(metrics)) {
    triggerOfflineRetrain();
  }
}, 3600000);
```

## Why This Is Asked

